/-
# A 2-generated infinite simple amenable group exists (AimPL Amenability of discrete groups, 4.65)

AimPL, Amenability of discrete groups, Problem 4.65 (repeated as Problem 4.7): is there a
2-generated infinite simple amenable group?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple
public import MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AmenableGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGeneratedSimpleAmenableAIMGeometricGroupTheoryProblem121Wanted

/-!
Source: AimPL: Amenability of discrete groups, Problem 4.65 (= Problem 4.7),
http://aimpl.org/amenablediscrete/4/. UnsolvedMath record UM-20001612
(`AIM-GEOMETRIC_GROUP_THEORY-0121`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Amenability is MathlibExt's `IsAmenable` (the Følner condition, equivalent to amenability for
discrete groups). 2-generated: two elements generate the group.
-/

/-- AimPL Problem 4.65 (Amenability of discrete groups): there is an infinite simple amenable group
(`IsAmenable` of MathlibExt, the Følner condition) generated by two elements. -/
def existsTwoGeneratedInfiniteSimpleAmenableGroup : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), IsAmenable G ∧ IsSimpleGroup G ∧ Infinite G ∧
    ∃ a b : G, Subgroup.closure {a, b} = ⊤

/--
Resolved true: Kionke and Schesler (Theorem 1.1 = Theorem 9.13) constructed an infinite 2-generated
amenable residually finite group with an infinite simple quotient, the head of a telescope of
alternating groups; the quotient is 2-generated, infinite, simple and amenable, answering the AimPL
question affirmatively, as they state. Source: AimPL: Amenability of discrete groups, Problem 4.65
(= Problem 4.7), http://aimpl.org/amenablediscrete/4/; resolution: S. Kionke and E. Schesler, From
telescopes to frames and simple groups, J. Comb. Algebra (2024), arXiv:2304.09307, Section 1:
Juschenko's question whether 2-generated infinite simple amenable groups exist, 'see also [AimPL,
Problem 4.7]', is answered affirmatively by Theorem 1.1 (= Theorem 9.13): there is an infinite
2-generated amenable residually finite group G which admits an infinite simple quotient Q (Q is
2-generated and amenable as a quotient of G), https://doi.org/10.4171/JCA/103.
-/
public theorem_wanted existsTwoGeneratedInfiniteSimpleAmenableGroup_holds :
    existsTwoGeneratedInfiniteSimpleAmenableGroup

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TwoGeneratedSimpleAmenableAIMGeometricGroupTheoryProblem121Wanted
